<title>BELGIUM: Tourism Council cancelled.</title>
<headline>Tourism Council cancelled.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The planned November 5 Tourism Council has been cancelled because of a lack of points of substance to discuss, a European Union source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was uncertain whether there would be any Tourism Council at all during the Irish presidency, he said.</p>
<p>The Council was first postponed from October 24 to next Tuesday before being cancelled without any new date set.</p>
<p>The only point on the agenda would have been the Commission's proposal on a first multiannual programme to assist European tourism in 1997 to 2000.</p>
<p>The source said this was a controversial point for some member states.</p>
</text>
